u$ for which either the space of traces contains a~degenerate nonzero trace $tr_{
u}$ or the space of supertraces contains a~degenerate nonzero supertrace $str_{
u}$ and, as a~consequence, the algebra $\mathcal H$ has two-sided ideals: one consisting of all vectors in the kernel of the form $B_{tr_{
u}}(x,y)=tr_{
u}(xy)$ or another consisting of all vectors in the kernel of the form $B_{str_{
